{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 20 worlds: the distributor with switches for two contextual uncertainties (supplier capacity and outage; volatile demand with impatient customers). With all switches at 0 it equals ch20-distributor. Base model: a distributor facing a demand jump of uncertain size, with uncertain supply and forecasting delays. Two ordering policies: ignore the supply line (weight 0) or count it (weight 1). }
Base Demand=
	100
	~	case/week
	~	Customer orders per week before the jump.
	|
Demand Jump=
	0.2
	~	dmnl
	~	Fractional rise in demand at week 10 (uncertain).
	|
Demand Pattern=
	Base Demand * (1 + STEP(Demand Jump, 10) - Volatile Demand * STEP(Demand Reversal, 30) + Volatile Demand * Season Amplitude * SIN(6.28319 * Time / Season Period))
	~	case/week
	~	Orders customers would place if delivery were normal: a step, or (volatile world) a surge, a reversal and a season.
	|
Volatile Demand=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	World switch: 1 adds the reversal, the season and impatient customers.
	|
Demand Reversal=
	0.5
	~	dmnl
	~	Fall in demand at week 30 in the volatile world.
	|
Season Amplitude=
	0.15
	~	dmnl
	~	Seasonal swing in the volatile world.
	|
Season Period=
	26
	~	week
	~	Length of the seasonal cycle.
	|
Customer Impatience=
	1.5
	~	dmnl
	~	How strongly customers go elsewhere when delivery is slow (volatile world only).
	|
Perceived Delivery Delay=
	SMOOTHI(Backlog / MAX(Shipments, 1), 1, Target Delivery Time)
	~	week
	~	Delivery delay as customers experience it.
	|
Effect of Delay on Demand=
	EXP(-Volatile Demand * Customer Impatience * MAX(0, Perceived Delivery Delay / Target Delivery Time - 1))
	~	dmnl
	~	Share of would-be orders that stay when delivery is slower than normal.
	|
Customer Demand=
	Demand Pattern * Effect of Delay on Demand
	~	case/week
	~	Orders arriving from customers.
	|
Lost Orders= INTEG(
	Demand Pattern - Customer Demand,
	0)
	~	case
	~	Orders customers took elsewhere because delivery was slow.
	|
Backlog= INTEG(
	Customer Demand - Orders Filled,
	Normal Backlog)
	~	case
	~	Customer orders received but not yet shipped.
	|
Target Delivery Time=
	2
	~	week
	~	Normal time from customer order to shipment.
	|
Desired Shipments=
	Backlog / Target Delivery Time
	~	case/week
	~	Shipments needed to keep the normal delivery time.
	|
Minimum Shipping Time=
	1
	~	week
	~	Fastest the warehouse can ship its whole inventory.
	|
Shipments=
	MIN(Desired Shipments, Inventory / Minimum Shipping Time)
	~	case/week
	~	Limited by what is in stock.
	|
Orders Filled=
	Shipments
	~	case/week
	~	Customer orders leave the backlog as their goods are shipped.
	|
Inventory= INTEG(
	Arrivals - Shipments,
	Target Inventory)
	~	case
	~	Cases in the warehouse.
	|
Inventory Coverage=
	2
	~	week
	~	Weeks of expected demand the distributor wants on hand.
	|
Forecast Time=
	4
	~	week
	~	Averaging time for expected demand (uncertain).
	|
Expected Demand=
	SMOOTH(Customer Demand, Forecast Time)
	~	case/week
	~	Smoothed customer demand used for ordering.
	|
Target Inventory=
	Expected Demand * Inventory Coverage
	~	case
	~	Inventory the distributor aims for.
	|
Supply Delay=
	4
	~	week
	~	Actual average time from order to arrival (uncertain).
	|
Quoted Lead Time=
	4
	~	week
	~	The lead time the supplier quotes.
	|
Lead Time Measured=
	1
	~	dmnl
	~	Policy switch: 1 uses the measured actual delay, 0 uses the quoted lead time.
	|
Believed Supply Delay=
	Lead Time Measured * MIN(Measured Supply Delay, Delay Cap) + (1 - Lead Time Measured) * Quoted Lead Time
	~	week
	~	The delay the ordering policy uses for the desired supply line.
	|
Desired Supply Line=
	Expected Demand * Believed Supply Delay
	~	case
	~	Orders that should be on the way, using the believed delay.
	|
Delay Cap=
	1000
	~	week
	~	Policy: the longest lead time the planner will plan for when counting the supply line (1000 means no cap).
	|
Adjustment Time=
	2
	~	week
	~	Time over which inventory and supply line gaps are corrected (uncertain).
	|
Supply Line Weight=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	Policy: 0 ignores orders on the way, 1 counts them fully.
	|
Orders=
	MAX(0, Expected Demand + (Target Inventory - Inventory) / Adjustment Time + Supply Line Weight * (Desired Supply Line - Supply Line) / Adjustment Time)
	~	case/week
	~	Orders placed with the supplier.
	|
Supply Line= INTEG(
	Orders - Arrivals,
	Expected Demand * Supply Delay)
	~	case
	~	Cases ordered but not yet received.
	|
Arrivals=
	MIN(Supply Line / Supply Delay, Supplier Capacity)
	~	case/week
	~	Deliveries from the supplier, limited by its capacity in the fragile-supply world.
	|
Fragile Supply=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	World switch: 1 gives the supplier a capacity limit and an outage.
	|
Normal Supplier Capacity=
	150
	~	case/week
	~	What the supplier can ship to this distributor in the fragile world.
	|
Outage Depth=
	0.6
	~	dmnl
	~	Share of supplier capacity lost during the outage.
	|
Outage Start=
	20
	~	week
	~	When the outage begins.
	|
Outage Duration=
	6
	~	week
	~	How long the outage lasts.
	|
Supplier Capacity=
	Fragile Supply * Normal Supplier Capacity * (1 - Outage Depth * PULSE(Outage Start, Outage Duration)) + (1 - Fragile Supply) * Unlimited Capacity
	~	case/week
	~	Shipping capacity of the supplier (effectively unlimited when supply is dependable).
	|
Unlimited Capacity=
	1e+06
	~	case/week
	~	Stands for no capacity limit.
	|
Measured Supply Delay=
	SMOOTHI(Supply Line / MAX(Arrivals, 0.001), 2, Supply Delay)
	~	week
	~	Lead time the planner measures: cases on order divided by cases arriving, averaged over two weeks.
	|
Holding Cost Rate=
	1
	~	dollar/case/week
	~	Cost of keeping a case in stock for a week.
	|
Backlog Cost Rate=
	5
	~	dollar/case/week
	~	Cost of a customer order waiting one week beyond normal.
	|
Normal Backlog=
	Customer Demand * Target Delivery Time
	~	case
	~	Backlog that corresponds to the normal delivery time.
	|
Excess Backlog=
	MAX(0, Backlog - Normal Backlog)
	~	case
	~	Orders waiting beyond the normal delivery time.
	|
Lost Margin=
	20
	~	dollar/case
	~	Margin lost on each order a customer takes elsewhere.
	|
Cost Rate=
	Holding Cost Rate * Inventory + Backlog Cost Rate * Excess Backlog + Lost Margin * (Demand Pattern - Customer Demand)
	~	dollar/week
	~	Weekly cost of stock and of late orders.
	|
Total Cost= INTEG(
	Cost Rate,
	0)
	~	dollar
	~	Cost accumulated over the horizon.
	|
********************************************************
	.Control
********************************************************~
		Simulation Control Parameters
	|
FINAL TIME  = 60
	~	week
	~	The final time for the simulation.
	|
INITIAL TIME  = 0
	~	week
	~	The initial time for the simulation.
	|
SAVEPER  = 
        TIME STEP
	~	week [0,?]
	~	The frequency with which output is stored.
	|
TIME STEP  = 0.0625
	~	week [0,?]
	~	The time step for the simulation.
	|
